# H, the holder matrix: who bears the remainder, and how much of it. One row per
# (filing, layer, kind), which is the sparse form of an L x 5 matrix. No row means that
# kind bears nothing, or that nobody said. The two readings are not separated here, which
# is what `share_absent` is for.
#
# A distribution, not a selection
#   One remainder routinely lands on several parties at once: the firm books part of it, a
#   counterparty absorbs part under contract, and a customer waits for the rest. A single "who
#   absorbs this" column would have forced the filer to pick one, and picking one is the
#   flattening the tall table refuses.
#
# Only `counterparty` names a party and a date
#   It is the only kind whose bearer is a third party with an agreement behind it. The schema
#   enforces both directions of that: no other kind may name one, and a counterparty must.
-- pm:Remainder/pm:holder; kind is pm:HolderKind.
SELECT h.filing, h.layer, h.kind,
       h.share_low, h.share_mode, h.share_high, h.share_unit, h.share_absent,
       h.party, h.as_of, h.share_derivation
FROM pm.holder h
